+## 3. What to do next, in order
+
+### 3.1 Fix the `agent-registration` v1 MISMATCH (PR #76, branch `lane-a/A-3.1a-registration-contract` @36f7943)
+
+**The MISMATCH from Lane B** (board, 2026-10-12 21:41):
+- `schemas.json#/definitions/ownerInstallationList` caps `installations` at `maxItems: 6`.
+- But handoffs.md §6.5 allows several active legacy installations plus up to five ended ones.
+- So a valid seven-item list (two active legacy + five ended) is rejected.
+
+**The fix**
+- Remove that `maxItems: 6`, or replace it with a generous safety bound.
+- Express the "≤ 5 ended" rule in the fixture test, since JSON Schema can't count by status.
+- Add a fixture with two active legacy + five ended installations.
+
+**Version decision, which is the human's.** The precedent is a3 MISMATCH round 1, where a fixture/schema error was fixed within the same version with a revision note. Record it in the contract's "Revisions within v1", then:
+1. run an independent review;
+2. post `CONTRACT-PUBLISHED agent-registration v1 @<sha>` (corrected);
+3. ask Lane B to re-run #78 and ACK;
+4. the human re-approves.
+
+**Read #76 in full first.** Another session wrote it, and this session never reviewed it. It is a large contract with 68 fixtures. Run your own independent review: the approval came before any Lane B review.
